<chapter xml:id="ch-what-one-method-cannot-show" xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">
  <title>What One Method Cannot Show</title>

  <introduction>
    <p>
      The fonio account examines questions about farming and household systems that agronomic experiments alone cannot settle. Different enquiries contribute distinct evidence. David's recognition that observational research was harder to support than he expected opens questions about purpose, expertise, training and team composition.
    </p>
  </introduction>

  <section xml:id="sec-what-one-method-cannot-show-source-notes">
    <title>Source notes</title>
    <p>
      <alert>Writing note:</alert> Keep the remembered survey and farmer explanations appropriately attributed; do not imply that the experiments failed or invent a completed observational study.
    </p>
    <p>
      <alert>Main transcripts:</alert> RMS and Observational Studies; Multimethod Agricultural Research.
    </p>
    <p>
      <alert>Supporting:</alert> On-farm Agricultural Trials; One Year or More; Crop Simulation Models, through a brief reference to <xref ref="ch-let-the-study-learn"/>.
    </p>
  </section>
</chapter>
